  "question": {
    "text": "The de Broglie wavelength of an electron having kinetic energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>. If the kinetic energy of electron becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>E</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>, then its de-Broglie wavelength will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>&#955;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The de-Broglie wavelength in the first case is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>E</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>In the second case the kinetic energy is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>E</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Let the de-Broglie wavelength be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>.</p><p>The value of wavelength is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>E</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>E</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
